WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:01.960
Luke 5

00:01.960 --> 00:07.680
On one occasion, while the crowd was pressing in on him to hear the word of God,

00:08.140 --> 00:12.440
he was standing by the lake of Gennesaret, and he saw two boats by the lake,

00:12.860 --> 00:16.120
but the fishermen had gone out of them and were washing their nets.

00:16.940 --> 00:19.440
Getting into one of the boats, which was Simon's,

00:19.700 --> 00:22.040
he asked him to put out a little from the land,

00:22.460 --> 00:24.880
and he sat down and taught the people from the boat.

00:25.560 --> 00:28.600
And when he had finished speaking, he said to Simon,

00:28.600 --> 00:32.640
Put out into the deep, and let down your nets for a catch.

00:33.260 --> 00:34.740
And Simon answered,

00:35.260 --> 00:39.500
Master, we toiled all night and took nothing,

00:40.240 --> 00:43.380
but at your word I will let down the nets.

00:44.160 --> 00:47.720
And when they had done this, they enclosed a large number of fish,

00:47.960 --> 00:49.260
and their nets were breaking.

00:50.200 --> 00:53.460
They signaled to their partners in the other boat to come and help them,

00:53.860 --> 00:57.600
and they came and filled both the boats, so that they began to sink.

00:57.600 --> 01:02.800
But when Simon Peter saw it, he fell down at Jesus' knees, saying,

01:03.540 --> 01:08.080
Depart from me, for I am a sinful man, O Lord.

01:08.860 --> 01:13.240
For he and all who were with him were astonished at the catch of fish that they had taken.

01:13.840 --> 01:18.700
And so also were James and John, sons of Zebedee, who were partners with Simon.

01:19.340 --> 01:20.840
And Jesus said to Simon,

01:21.320 --> 01:25.300
Do not be afraid. From now on you will be catching men.

01:25.720 --> 01:27.580
And when they had brought their boats to land,

01:27.600 --> 01:30.020
they left everything and followed him.

01:31.120 --> 01:35.380
While he was in one of the cities, there came a man full of leprosy.

01:35.880 --> 01:39.600
And when he saw Jesus, he fell on his face and begged him,

01:40.280 --> 01:44.520
Lord, if you will, you can make me clean.

01:45.340 --> 01:48.220
And Jesus stretched out his hand and touched him, saying,

01:48.900 --> 01:51.080
I will be clean.

01:51.560 --> 01:54.120
And immediately the leprosy left him,

01:54.460 --> 01:57.080
and he charged him to tell no one but,

01:57.600 --> 01:59.860
Go, and show yourself to the priest,

02:00.160 --> 02:02.660
and make an offering for your cleansing, as Moses commanded,

02:03.140 --> 02:04.100
for a proof to them.

02:04.780 --> 02:07.600
But now even more the report about him went abroad,

02:07.920 --> 02:12.180
and great crowds gathered to hear him and to be healed of their infirmities.

02:12.880 --> 02:15.900
But he would withdraw to desolate places and pray.

02:17.180 --> 02:19.880
On one of those days, as he was teaching,

02:20.460 --> 02:22.840
Pharisees and teachers of the law were sitting there,

02:22.840 --> 02:27.560
who had come from every village of Galilee and Judea and from Jerusalem,

02:28.260 --> 02:30.780
and the power of the Lord was with him to heal.

02:31.540 --> 02:35.520
And behold, some men were bringing on a bed a man who was paralyzed,

02:36.000 --> 02:39.040
and they were seeking to bring him in and lay him before Jesus.

02:39.520 --> 02:42.300
But finding no way to bring him in because of the crowd,

02:42.700 --> 02:45.620
they went up on the roof and let him down with his bed

02:45.620 --> 02:48.320
through the tiles into the midst before Jesus.

02:49.020 --> 02:51.520
And when he saw their faith, he said,

02:52.180 --> 02:55.240
Man, your sins are forgiven you.

02:55.900 --> 02:57.500
And the scribes and the Pharisees,

02:57.600 --> 02:59.260
they began to question, saying,

03:00.040 --> 03:02.160
Who is this who speaks blasphemies?

03:02.480 --> 03:04.820
Who can forgive sins but God alone?

03:05.460 --> 03:08.920
When Jesus perceived their thoughts, he answered them,

03:09.460 --> 03:11.880
Why do you question in your hearts?

03:12.580 --> 03:15.380
Which is easier to say, your sins are forgiven you,

03:15.480 --> 03:17.500
or to say, rise and walk?

03:18.120 --> 03:22.120
But that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins,

03:22.420 --> 03:24.720
he said to the man who was paralyzed,

03:25.260 --> 03:27.560
I say to you, rise,

03:27.920 --> 03:30.040
pick up your bed, and go home.

03:30.780 --> 03:32.840
And immediately he rose up before them

03:32.840 --> 03:34.720
and picked up what he had been lying on,

03:34.900 --> 03:36.880
and went home glorifying God.

03:37.500 --> 03:39.600
And amazement seized them all,

03:40.160 --> 03:43.780
and they glorified God and were filled with awe, saying,

03:44.520 --> 03:46.860
We have seen extraordinary things today.

03:48.760 --> 03:52.000
After this he went out and saw a tax collector named Levi

03:52.000 --> 03:53.440
sitting at the tax booth.

03:54.040 --> 03:55.340
And he said to him,

03:56.060 --> 03:56.960
Follow me.

03:57.600 --> 04:00.160
And leaving everything, he rose and followed him.

04:00.700 --> 04:03.360
And Levi made him a great feast in his house.

04:03.720 --> 04:06.180
And there was a large company of tax collectors

04:06.180 --> 04:08.600
and others reclining at table with them.

04:09.220 --> 04:12.660
And the Pharisees and their scribes grumbled at his disciples, saying,

04:13.080 --> 04:18.500
Why do you eat and drink with tax collectors and sinners?

04:19.580 --> 04:21.240
And Jesus answered them,

04:22.020 --> 04:24.520
Those who are well have no need of a physician,

04:24.880 --> 04:26.000
but those who are sick.

04:26.540 --> 04:27.580
I have not come to call you,

04:27.580 --> 04:29.880
but sinners to repentance.

04:30.900 --> 04:31.960
And they said to him,

04:32.740 --> 04:35.500
The disciples of John fast often and offer prayers,

04:35.780 --> 04:37.620
and so do the disciples of the Pharisees,

04:37.920 --> 04:39.540
but yours eat and drink.

04:40.260 --> 04:41.500
And Jesus said to them,

04:42.320 --> 04:45.300
Can you make wedding guests fast while the bridegroom is with them?

04:46.100 --> 04:49.000
The days will come when the bridegroom is taken away from them,

04:49.340 --> 04:51.780
and then they will fast in those days.

04:52.280 --> 04:54.280
He also told them a parable.

04:55.040 --> 04:57.080
No one tears a piece from a new garment

04:57.080 --> 04:57.560
and puts it on a new one.

04:57.560 --> 05:00.800
If he does, he will tear the new,

05:00.920 --> 05:02.980
and the piece from the new will not match the old.

05:03.660 --> 05:06.860
And no one puts new wine into old wineskins.

05:07.300 --> 05:10.060
If he does, the new wine will burst the skins,

05:10.160 --> 05:12.820
and it will be spilled, and the skins will be destroyed.

05:13.600 --> 05:16.640
But new wine must be put into fresh wineskins,

05:17.220 --> 05:19.780
and no one after drinking old wine desires new,

05:20.200 --> 05:23.380
for he says, The old is good.

